; Stage 2b: line over 127 characters (readline splits it), Latin-1
; umlauts and $FD-$FF from the file; typed umlauts (MapANSI, German keymap)
; in a new first line; SAVE.
; TED-C tokenises the first part of the split line like the other lines
; (the original TED leaves it text, #376), and it splits the line after
; 128 characters without losing the 3 bytes the original drops at its cut
; after 127 (#375), and it loads each Latin-1 byte of the text file as one
; character - the umlauts as typing stores them (26-31), the others with
; bit 7 cleared by the tokeniser - where the original took it and the
; byte behind it as a token pair (#374; R5-C5 and Rc-Cc are named for #376
; already).
; @fixed #376 R5-C5 Rc-Cc
; @source E long_umlaut
; @expect bak long_umlaut.bb2.bak
; @expect exists long_umlaut.bb2
; @est 6
timeout 10
wait req "OKEE DOKEE"
gad 1
wait screen
dump start
menu 2 0
type "; äöü ÄÖÜ ß\n"
dump typed
menu 0 2
wait freq "Name to save file as"
freq ok
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
